::<b>Ack Basswards II</b>

<b>You can take the government out of politics, but not the politics out of government.</b>



Junker vs. Junkerin? Junker is a Junker, man type. <nowiki>Junkerin</nowiki> is a Junker, female type. <nowiki>JunkerIn</nowiki> is common unisex ideography, male or female type. So, I am Junker or in Germany Junker or Junkerin. The meaning of Junker, in German, is mostly of historical significance.

Since I am now producing ISP or Hosting reviews, I'll add my computer background here.
:High school: handheld calculator 'programming' when they were not 'handheld' rather as big as a refrigerator.
:College: ASU, 1yr comp. sci. major, then split. Programmed Fortran, Cobol, & Basic (Univac 1110 & netted TTYs).
:Autodidact: 1st PC, 1977, home assembled. Programmed Z-80 assembler & Basic. 2nd PC Radio Shack something. Programmed 8080? assembler, Basic. 3rd PC, 1983, IBM PC. Programmed Turbo Pascal, 80x86 assembler. Along the way, also Forth, and Lisp. At work I spent a couple years doing toolbook scripting & whatever it was called on the Mac. Since then, several PCs as they got faster & faster. I went internet late, prob 2000. I run two net sites, soon to be three, & do my own html, etc.

<b>Junker Email</b> - junker(at)rlmcom(dot)com

